;; Declarations outside the world (A8 and A8b of the Ghidra case study's G1 plan; J2G-SPEC §4.1, "Declarations
;; outside the world"): a Java program whose classes name a JDK module outside the Go build's world (java.desktop's
;; java.beans and java.awt.Desktop, java.sql's javax.sql.DataSource) and a binary-only jar on javac's class path
;; alone (org.example:toyext:1.0, test/java/project/make-jars'), each in code the main run does not execute.
;; With :outside the classes are translated, not refused (A7's), and each operation on an outside class throws
;; when reached, naming its source: the runs reach and reach-jar are the negative controls (they fail loudly).
{:main-class demo.outside.Main
 :roots :entry
 :java {:release 25
        :repository "../java-project/maven"
        :outside [:platform :class-path]
        :modules [{:name "app" :src ["src"] :artifacts ["org.example:toyext:1.0"]}]}}
